IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part7-overseas`

-- Tests for Part 7 (regulations 21 to 23, lines 274 to 307). Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Part 7`

§§ `Regulation 21(6): the specified territory`

-- Any part of the Channel Islands not subject to an Order under section 179 of the Administration Act.
#ASSERT `the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` TRUE `given` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` TRUE `given` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` FALSE `given` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)` FALSE `given` TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 21: what happens to an up-rating increase`

GIVEN made IS A BOOLEAN
      deferred IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled at end` IS A BOOLEAN
      `overseas at end` IS A BOOLEAN
      falls IS A `When an up-rating increase falls against the deferral period`
      `overseas at time` IS A BOOLEAN
      continued IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an up-rating increase for a person abroad`
`an increase` made deferred `entitled at end` `overseas at end` falls `overseas at time` continued `entitled before` MEANS
    `Facts about an up-rating increase for a person abroad` WITH
        `Regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to the up-rating increase` IS made
        `the person's entitlement to a state pension had been deferred for a period` IS deferred
        `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS `entitled at end`
        `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident` IS `overseas at end`
        `where the increase falls against the deferral period` IS falls
        `the person was an overseas resident at the time of the increase` IS `overseas at time`
        `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended` IS continued
        `the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase` IS `entitled before`

`taken away` MEANS `regulation 21 takes the increase away from the person`
`kept` MEANS `regulation 21 does not take the increase away from the person`
`not applied` MEANS `regulation 21 does not apply to this increase, because no Regulations have been made applying it`
`respect` MEANS `in respect of the deferral period`
`after` MEANS `after the deferral period ended`
`other` MEANS `at some other time`

-- (2): without Regulations applying it, regulation 21 does nothing.
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `not applied`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `after` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `not applied`
-- (5), "in all other cases" (never deferred): lost if entitled immediately before and an overseas resident.
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `taken away`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `kept`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `kept`
-- (3) does not apply: deferred, but not entitled at the end of the deferral period, or not then an overseas resident: back to (5).
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `after` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `taken away`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `after` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `taken away`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `after` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `kept`
-- (3), (4)(a): an increase in respect of the deferral period is lost if the person was an overseas resident at the time and stayed one
-- until the deferral period ended. Entitlement before the increase is not required in (4).
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `respect` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `taken away`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `respect` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `kept`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `respect` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `kept`
-- (3), (4)(b): an increase after the deferral period is lost if the person is an overseas resident at the time of it.
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `after` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `taken away`
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `after` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `kept`
-- (3), (4): an increase at some other time is not within (4)(a) or (b), and (5) is for "all other cases", so it is not lost.
#ASSERT `what regulation 21 does to an up-rating increase` (`an increase` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `other` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `kept`

§§ `Regulation 22: which weekly rate an increment is a percentage of`

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
      overseas IS A BOOLEAN
      `in gb` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not`
`a part` first last overseas `in gb` MEANS
    `A part of the deferral period, abroad or not` WITH
        `the first day of the part` IS first
        `the last day of the part` IS last
        `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS overseas
        `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS `in gb`

`at the start` MEANS `the weekly rate immediately before the start of the part`
`at the end` MEANS `the weekly rate immediately before the end of the part`
`unsaid` MEANS `the Regulations do not say, because the person was an overseas resident who was in Great Britain or a specified territory`

-- (3): not an overseas resident: the rate immediately before the end of the part; whether in Great Britain does not matter.
#ASSERT `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `at the end`
#ASSERT `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `at the end`
-- (2): an overseas resident not in Great Britain or a specified territory: the rate immediately before the start of the part.
#ASSERT `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `at the start`
-- An overseas resident in Great Britain or a specified territory is in neither (2) nor (3).
#ASSERT `which weekly rate the increment for a part is a percentage of` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `unsaid`

-- The rates: 230 at the start of the part and 240 at the end.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to for a part` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE TRUE) `given the rate at the start` 230 `and the rate at the end` 240 EQUALS JUST 240
#ASSERT `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to for a part` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE FALSE) `given the rate at the start` 230 `and the rate at the end` 240 EQUALS JUST 230
#ASSERT `the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to for a part` (`a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE TRUE) `given the rate at the start` 230 `and the rate at the end` 240 EQUALS NOTHING

-- The increment is the percentage (one-ninth of 1%) of that rate: 900 gives 1.
#ASSERT `the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` 900 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` 241.30 EQUALS 241.30 TIMES (1 / 900)

-- (1): the regulation applies if the person has been an overseas resident in any part of the deferral period.
#ASSERT `regulation 22 applies to the deferral period` (LIST `a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE TRUE, `a part` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 22 applies to the deferral period` (LIST `a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 22 applies to the deferral period` EMPTY)

§§ `Regulation 23: both regulations 12A and 22 apply`

-- (1): section 17(4) falls to be modified under both: there is a non-uprating change (12A) and an overseas part (22).
`the whole of 2026` MEANS `Deferral period` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 31 12 2026
#ASSERT `regulation 23 applies to` `the whole of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 7 2026) `and the parts` (LIST `a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 23 applies to` `the whole of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` EMPTY `and the parts` (LIST `a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 23 applies to` `the whole of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 7 2026) `and the parts` (LIST `a part` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE TRUE))
-- (3) to (5): the first increment is the percentage of the regulation 22 rate; the change under (4) is nil when 12A(2) is read with
-- the same rate (fork F20), so the increment under regulation 23 is the first increment.
#ASSERT `the increment under regulation 23, the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to being` 900 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the increment under regulation 23, the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to being` 450 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the increment under regulation 23, the weekly rate regulation 22 refers to being` 450 EQUALS `the increment under regulation 22, the weekly rate being` 450
